---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="No Keyboard for That Language? Just Say It. — FusionMD & PolyWrite"
  description="You don't need a Japanese IME or an Arabic keyboard layout to write in another language. macOS Dictation types it for you as you speak it — and for the sentences that really need to land right, saying them beats translating them."
>

  <div class="guide-wrap">

    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="guide-hero fade-in">
      <div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/tutorials">← Tutorials</a></div>
      <div class="hero-badge">DataIsland Publishing Guide</div>
      <h1>No Keyboard for That Language? Just Say It.</h1>
      <p class="hero-sub">
        You don't need to learn an input method or hunt for accented characters to write
        a sentence in a language you don't have a keyboard for. macOS Dictation transcribes
        speech straight into FusionMD or PolyWrite, in the right script, automatically. And
        for the lines that really need to land right, speaking them yourself skips the layer
        where machine translation tends to introduce mistakes.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-meta">
        Covers: macOS Dictation &nbsp;·&nbsp; speaking versus translating &nbsp;·&nbsp; FusionMD & PolyWrite
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Part 1 -->
    <section class="guide-section fade-in" id="p1">
      <div class="part-num">Part 1</div>
      <h2>The keyboard isn't the only way in</h2>
      <p>
        Plenty of people can speak a second or third language passably — or know someone,
        a colleague, a friend, a family member, who can — without wanting to memorize a
        Japanese IME or an Arabic keyboard layout for the sake of a single email. Typing
        was never really the requirement; getting the right words into the document was.
        macOS Dictation removes the input problem entirely: speak, and the words appear
        already in the correct script — right-to-left, accented, tone marks and all —
        without adding a new keyboard layout you'll never use again.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Part 2 -->
    <section class="guide-section fade-in" id="p2">
      <div class="part-num">Part 2</div>
      <h2>Turn on Dictation for the language you need</h2>
      <p>
        In <strong>System Settings → Keyboard → Dictation</strong>, turn Dictation on and
        set the language you'll be speaking in. If you need to switch languages between
        messages, that's where you switch it.
      </p>
      <p>
        In <strong>FusionMD</strong> or <strong>PolyWrite</strong>: click into the document
        where you want the text, then press <strong>Fn Fn</strong> (or choose
        <strong>Edit → Start Dictation</strong>) and speak. The words land in the document
        exactly like typed text — same font, same paragraph — ready for spell-check,
        formatting, and export like anything else you wrote.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Part 3 -->
    <section class="guide-section fade-in" id="p3">
      <div class="part-num">Part 3</div>
      <h2>Why speaking beats translating, for the parts that matter</h2>
      <p>
        Our <a href="/tutorials/international-trade">Writing for International Trade</a> guide
        covers writing in English or French and using on-device translation to convert it to
        your partner's language — fast, and good enough for routine correspondence. But a
        translation is still a second-hand version of what you meant, generated by a model
        guessing at your intent. Idiom, tone, and register are exactly the things machine
        translation still gets subtly wrong — and if you don't read the target language
        well, you have no way to catch it before you send it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Dictation skips that layer. If you — or a bilingual colleague, or a native-speaking
        contact on the phone — can just say the sentence in the target language, what lands
        in the document is the actual sentence someone meant, not a translation's best guess
        at it.
      </p>
      <div class="callout-block">
        <strong>This isn't an argument against translation.</strong> For an entire document
        in a language you don't speak a word of, translation is still the only practical
        option. Dictation is specifically for the handful of lines — a closing statement,
        a specific offer, an apology, a condolence — where getting the exact words right
        matters more than getting the whole document done fast.
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Part 4 -->
    <section class="guide-section fade-in" id="p4">
      <div class="part-num">Part 4</div>
      <h2>Use both together</h2>
      <p>
        Draft the bulk of a document in your working language, machine translate it as
        covered in <a href="/tutorials/international-trade">Writing for International Trade</a>,
        then dictate directly over the specific lines that need to be exact — yourself, or
        with a native speaker on the line reading it back to you. Select the translated
        sentence in FusionMD or PolyWrite, start Dictation, and speak the replacement; no
        re-formatting needed, it drops straight into the existing paragraph.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Who this serves -->
    <section class="guide-section fade-in" id="p5">
      <div class="part-num">Part 5</div>
      <h2>Who this is for</h2>
      <div class="checklist-grid">
        <div class="check-item">
          <span class="check-icon">✓</span>
          <div>
            <strong>Anyone messaging family or contacts abroad</strong>
            <p>Write a real letter home without fumbling accented characters or a script you've never typed before.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="check-item">
          <span class="check-icon">✓</span>
          <div>
            <strong>Businesses closing a deal</strong>
            <p>Where the exact wording of one line — a figure, an offer, a commitment — matters more than the rest of the document.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="check-item">
          <span class="check-icon">✓</span>
          <div>
            <strong>Writers including authentic dialogue or quotes</strong>
            <p>Dictate a line in another language the way a native speaker would actually say it, not the way a translator guesses it.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="check-item">
          <span class="check-icon">✓</span>
          <div>
            <strong>Anyone with a bilingual friend or colleague on hand</strong>
            <p>Hand them the microphone instead of asking them to proofread a translation after the fact.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Closing CTA -->
    <section class="guide-cta fade-in">
      <h2>Your words, in their language, said the way you'd actually say them.</h2>
      <p>
        No new keyboard layout to learn, no cloud translation service required for the
        sentences that need to be exact.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-links">
        <a href="/products/fusionmd" class="cta-primary">Learn about FusionMD →</a>
        <a href="/products/polywrite" class="cta-primary">Learn about PolyWrite →</a>
        <a href="/tutorials/international-trade" class="cta-secondary">Writing for International Trade →</a>
      </div>
    </section>

  </div><!-- /guide-wrap -->

</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .guide-wrap {
    max-width: 820px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem 6rem;
  }

  .breadcrumb { font-size: 0.9rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }

  /* Hero */
  .guide-hero {
    padding: 2.5rem 0 3rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--gray-light);
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .hero-badge {
    display: inline-block;
    background: var(--blue);
    color: #fff;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 0.3em 0.8em;
    border-radius: 999px;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .guide-hero h1 {
    font-size: 2.75rem;
    line-height: 1.15;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .hero-sub {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--gray-dark);
    max-width: 640px;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .hero-meta {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--gray);
  }

  /* Sections */
  .guide-section {
    padding: 2.5rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--gray-light);
  }

  .part-num {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--blue);
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }

  .guide-section h2 {
    font-size: 1.7rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .guide-section p {
    font-size: 0.97rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .guide-section a {
    color: var(--blue);
  }

  /* Checklist */
  .checklist-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  .check-item {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    background: var(--gray-light);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 1rem;
  }

  .check-icon {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--blue);
    flex-shrink: 0;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-top: 0.1rem;
  }

  .check-item strong { font-size: 0.95rem; display: block; margin-bottom: 0.3rem; }
  .check-item p { font-size: 0.87rem !important; margin: 0 !important; color: var(--gray-dark); line-height: 1.5 !important; }

  /* Callout */
  .callout-block {
    background: var(--blue-light, rgba(0,102,255,0.06));
    border-left: 3px solid var(--blue);
    border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
    padding: 0.85rem 1rem;
    font-size: 0.93rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 1.25rem 0;
    color: var(--gray-dark);
  }

  /* CTA */
  .guide-cta {
    text-align: center;
    padding: 3.5rem 0 1rem;
  }

  .guide-cta h2 { font-size: 1.8rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
  .guide-cta p  { font-size: 1rem; color: var(--gray-dark); line-height: 1.7; max-width: 560px; margin: 0 auto 2rem; }

  .cta-links {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    justify-content: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .cta-primary {
    background: var(--blue);
    color: #fff;
    padding: 0.7rem 1.5rem;
    border-radius: 8px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .cta-primary:hover { background: #005fa3; }

  .cta-secondary {
    background: var(--gray-light);
    color: var(--gray-dark);
    padding: 0.7rem 1.5rem;
    border-radius: 8px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .cta-secondary:hover { background: #e0e0e0; }

  /* Responsive */
  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .checklist-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .guide-hero h1 { font-size: 2rem; }
  }
</style>
